/-!+# The signed single-component reduction: quotient and action deductions

These modules prove the group-theoretic deductions needed to analyze every
branch of A.3.18 for the ordinary component L ≤ I with O(I) = 1.
The residual branch gives θ(I) = L. In the nonsplit index-three branch,
an outside theta-generator would survive the three-prime-core quotient and
split the extension, again giving θ(I) = L. The central models common to
(3a) and (3b) are excluded because the component image is centerless.
An order-three element outside L acts outerly on its actual two-core quotient;
membership in the GL₃ or unitary action image then supplies the precise
published diagonal-action predicate, with compatible quotient coordinates.

This is not yet the full rank-one or signed-diagonal reduction. The remaining
model work must restrict the complete 1.1.5 list, connect the actual split and
nonsplit A.3.18 models to these deductions, and in the split case locate a
suitable actor in Y₊ = θ(M ∩ I). An actor in θ(I) alone is insufficient.
The genuine earlier source results remain inputs of the eventual assembly;
neither their classification conclusions nor these missing model deductions
are asserted here.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), 1.1.5(3)
(printed pp.501--503), A.3.18 (pp.51--52), and 15.3.37, 15.3.43
(pp.1135, 1139). The opposite signed congruences in the rank-one and
diagonal models are retained by the imported output interfaces.
-/
